DomainQL
--------

The packages io.github.qlivedev.graphql.* in qlive-api and qlive-graphql
are derived from DomainQL, Copyright 2018 Quinscape GmbH, licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    https://github.com/quinscape/domainql

Vendored from commit cea405177c684d16e68a3081f6efbd1dfbbd5204 of the
branch fix/timestamp-scalar-utc, which descends from master at
b90996a89bbca4e992ba6e35cdd0e90cec9cf0d2 and adds two fixes that were
never published upstream: the timestamp scalar serializing as the UTC it
claims, and a null jsonb column deserializing as null.

Changed from that commit:

  - repackaged from de.quinscape.domainql.* to io.github.qlivedev.graphql.*
  - split across two Maven modules, qlive-api and qlive-graphql
  - the DDL generation subsystem and its command line removed, along with
    the model and schema packages that only served it
  - the dependency on de.quinscape:spring-jsview replaced by QLive's own
    io.github.qlivedev.util.JSONUtil
  - built against graphql-java 25, jOOQ 3.19 and jakarta.servlet, where
    the original used graphql-java 20, jOOQ 3.17 and javax.servlet
  - GraphQL subscription support dropped; QLive pushes over its own
    websocket connection
  - tests migrated from JUnit 4 to JUnit Jupiter


babel-plugin-track-usage
------------------------

src/vite/babel in qlive-ts is derived from babel-plugin-track-usage,
Copyright Quinscape GmbH, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    https://github.com/quinscape/babel-plugin-track-usage

Vendored from commit 1aa8c7c451a3683390ba991e6a19e89dc1c5e5e2, whose
src/index.js and data.js are byte-identical to the published 0.3.4.

Changed from that commit:

  - converted from CommonJS to ES modules, and the unused fs import
    dropped with it
  - renamed to trackUsagePlugin.js and trackUsageData.js, with hand
    written .d.ts declarations beside them
  - src/dump.js not vendored: AST debugging scaffolding, already commented
    out at the call site, writing to an absolute path
  - the test suite ported from mocha and power-assert to vitest


